  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116208",
      "title": "Creating & Using an Observable",
      "lectureOrder": 210,
      "videoOrder": 201,
      "sourceHash": "bb133190892a99cb4c0e1cf27ed6fc27bc1a932517fdebe9fbd217263a2f8093",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 4.05,
          "en": "So in order to work with observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 6.75,
          "en": "and in order to create one ourselves,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.75,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "I prepared a brand new starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "which you find attached, as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "And if you then start that development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 18.27,
          "en": "after installing all dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.27,
          "end": 22.98,
          "en": "you should see this simple page here on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 26.25,
          "en": "And currently clicking this button won't do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "And of course the page isn't too exciting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 31.32,
          "en": "because in this section we'll not build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.32,
          "end": 33.78,
          "en": "some kind of demo project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.78,
          "end": 38.25,
          "en": "Instead we'll just play around with that observables feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.25,
          "end": 41.28,
          "en": "so that you get an idea of how it works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.28,
          "end": 43.65,
          "en": "and so that you know how you can work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.65,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "with observables if you encounter them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "as part of your Angular applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 52.65,
          "en": "Now as I mentioned before, you already saw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.65,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "one special kind of observable in action in the last section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 60.063,
          "en": "where we got started with this BehaviorSubject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.29,
          "end": 65.64,
          "en": "This is a feature provided by this RxJS library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.64,
          "end": 69.06,
          "en": "and the idea behind this subject, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.06,
          "end": 72.96000000000001,
          "en": "is an object that you can use to emit values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.96000000000001,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "to which you can then listen in another part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "of your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 80.76,
          "en": "kind of similar to how Signals work in Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.76,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "but you'll also learn about the difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "between these two concepts in this section here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "And subjects like this BehaviorSubject are, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "such a kind of observable because, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 98.58,
          "en": "with them you're creating and controlling a stream of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 101.16,
          "en": "to which you can then listen in another part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 103.08,
          "en": "of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.08,
          "end": 107.85,
          "en": "But subjects are just one way of creating observables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.85,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "The special kinds of observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "that act as event emitters, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 117.42,
          "en": "In this demo project I'll show you a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 120.693,
          "en": "of creating observables and working with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "And for that I'll start here in that app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 128.55,
          "en": "which is the only component I have in this dummy app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.55,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "And I'll start by implementing the OnInit interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 135.69,
          "en": "which must be imported from Angular core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.69,
          "end": 138.903,
          "en": "so that we're forced to add this ngOnInit method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 144.18,
          "en": "And in here I now wanna create a new observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.18,
          "end": 149.18,
          "en": "with help of that RxJS library without creating a subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 154.293,
          "en": "Instead, we can import something from RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 159.52,
          "en": "And that something could be the interval function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.07,
          "end": 164.76,
          "en": "because RxJS gives you multiple functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.76,
          "end": 168.12,
          "en": "you can use to create observables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.12,
          "end": 172.56,
          "en": "Now you can find a full list of all the functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.56,
          "end": 176.73,
          "en": "offered by this library and a description of what they do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 176.73,
          "end": 181.23,
          "en": "on the official website of this RxJS library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 183.18,
          "en": "And as an Angular developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.18,
          "end": 185.58,
          "en": "you don't need to know all these functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.58,
          "end": 189.33,
          "en": "and you also don't necessarily need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 192.36,
          "en": "a lot about RxJS if you don't want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.36,
          "end": 196.35,
          "en": "though I will say that there definitely are Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.35,
          "end": 201.35,
          "en": "developers and teams and projects that fully embrace RxJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.99,
          "end": 204.3,
          "en": "and might use it a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 204.3,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "But just to work with Angular, you don't need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 211.713,
          "en": "that much about it nowadays, in my opinion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 215.16,
          "en": "Nonetheless, here on this website, you for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 215.16,
          "end": 218.19,
          "en": "find details about this interval function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.19,
          "end": 221.34,
          "en": "And there you learn that this creates an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.34,
          "end": 226.32,
          "en": "that emits numbers every specified interval of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 226.32,
          "end": 231.183,
          "en": "And you then also find a usage example here on this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 236.16,
          "en": "So you could use this function now here in ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 237.75,
          "en": "and call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.75,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "And as a result you'd get back an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "that produces numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 246.03,
          "en": "That's what this generic type here tells you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 246.03,
          "end": 248.7,
          "en": "That's the type of value that will be managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.7,
          "end": 251.13,
          "en": "by this observable that is returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 251.13,
          "end": 252.693,
          "en": "by this interval function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.01,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "So unlike this BehaviorSubject we created before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 262.41,
          "en": "this observable created with help of interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.41,
          "end": 265.59,
          "en": "will now automatically produce values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 265.59,
          "end": 268.29,
          "en": "instead of doing that when we emit them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.29,
          "end": 270.72,
          "en": "which is what we did with the subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 270.72,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "Here the values will get produced automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 276.69,
          "en": "And we also can't really control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.69,
          "end": 280.29,
          "en": "which kind of value will be produced here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.29,
          "end": 282.75,
          "en": "And there are other creation methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 282.75,
          "end": 284.58,
          "en": "where you can control it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 284.58,
          "end": 288.003,
          "en": "but here, with interval, you don't have that much control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 291.6,
          "en": "Instead, here you just pass an argument to interval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 291.6,
          "end": 294.27,
          "en": "which defines the time in milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 294.27,
          "end": 296.82,
          "en": "after which a value will be produced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 296.82,
          "end": 301.113,
          "en": "So every 1,000 milliseconds a value would now be produced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 301.95,
          "end": 305.223,
          "en": "And then you can set up a subscription by calling subscribe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 306.15,
          "end": 309.63,
          "en": "just as you also saw it with the subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 313.05,
          "en": "So that's the same with any observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 313.05,
          "end": 317.1,
          "en": "In order to listen to the values that are emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 317.1,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "and in order to use them, you must set up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 325.41,
          "en": "Now, just as a side note here about subscribing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 325.41,
          "end": 327.45,
          "en": "you indeed need to subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 327.45,
          "end": 331.62,
          "en": "to kick off the observable, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 331.62,
          "end": 334.62,
          "en": "By default, when you call interval here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 334.62,
          "end": 338.25,
          "en": "it will not do anything unless you have a subscriber",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 338.25,
          "end": 342.51,
          "en": "because internally the RxJS library recognizes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 342.51,
          "end": 346.40999999999997,
          "en": "that if there's no one who's interested in the values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 346.40999999999997,
          "end": 349.26,
          "en": "it doesn't make sense to emit any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 349.26,
          "end": 351.78,
          "en": "So you need at least one subscriber",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 351.78,
          "end": 355.71,
          "en": "in order to really kick off this interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 355.71,
          "end": 358.08,
          "en": "This subscribe methods then takes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 358.08,
          "end": 361.92,
          "en": "a so-called observer object, which is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 361.92,
          "end": 366.24,
          "en": "that can implement up to three methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 366.24,
          "end": 369.54,
          "en": "A next method, or a next function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 369.54,
          "end": 370.86,
          "en": "however you want to call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 370.86,
          "end": 374.403,
          "en": "that will be triggered for every new value that's emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 375.81,
          "end": 379.83299999999997,
          "en": "And the emitted value will be received as a parameter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 380.94,
          "end": 383.82,
          "en": "And here we could then log that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 383.82,
          "end": 387.3,
          "en": "In addition, you could also implement a complete function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 387.3,
          "end": 391.59,
          "en": "which would be called if this observable would not emit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 391.59,
          "end": 395.94,
          "en": "any more numbers, though it depends on the observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 395.94,
          "end": 397.83,
          "en": "whether this will ever be triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 397.83,
          "end": 399.87,
          "en": "In case of the interval, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 399.87,
          "end": 402.54,
          "en": "it'll by default keep on emitting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 402.54,
          "end": 406.413,
          "en": "so the complete function might never execute there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 407.85,
          "end": 410.94,
          "en": "And you can also implement an error function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 410.94,
          "end": 414,
          "en": "which will be triggered if an error occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 414,
          "end": 417.65999999999997,
          "en": "which here, for this observable also shouldn't be the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 417.65999999999997,
          "end": 420.06,
          "en": "but which could be the case if you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 420.06,
          "end": 424.35,
          "en": "had an observable that's used for sending HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 424.35,
          "end": 427.47,
          "en": "and then providing the response of that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 427.47,
          "end": 430.29,
          "en": "Something you'll see later once we dive into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 430.29,
          "end": 434.25,
          "en": "sending HTTP requests with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 434.25,
          "end": 437.043,
          "en": "Here I'll only implement the next function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 438.24,
          "end": 441.78,
          "en": "And with that done, if you go back, reload your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 441.78,
          "end": 444.78,
          "en": "and open the Developer Tools, you'll see a new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 444.78,
          "end": 448.11,
          "en": "incrementing number being emitted every one second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 448.11,
          "end": 453.09000000000003,
          "en": "And that number is now produced by that interval observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 453.09000000000003,
          "end": 456.87,
          "en": "Now of course, this observable here isn't too useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 456.87,
          "end": 459.39,
          "en": "It could be though, if you had an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
